 and docosahexaenoic acid on lipid metabolism in black sea bream</article-title><source>Fish Sci</source><year>2003</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>1182</fpage><lpage>1193</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.0919-9268.2003.00744.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Om AD, Ji H, Umino T, Nakagawa H, Sasaki T, Okada K, Asano M, Nakagawa A (2003) Dietary effects of eicosapentaenoic acid and docosahexaenoic acid on lipid metabolism in black sea bream. Fish Sci 69:1182&#x02013;1193 </citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Puvanendran</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Kellett</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Parrish</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of enriched rotifers on growth, survival, and composition of larval Atlantic cod (<italic>Gadus morhua</italic>)</article-title><source>J Mar Sci</source><year>2006</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>285</fpage><lpage>295</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Park HG, Puvanendran V, Kellett A, Parrish CC, Brown JA (2006) Effect of enriched rotifers on growth, survival, and composition of larval Atlantic cod (Gadus morhua). J Mar Sci 63:285&#x02013;295 </citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pfeffer</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name><name><surname>Valentine</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Parrish</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Deuterium-induced differential isotope shift <sup>13</sup>C NMR-resonance reassignments of mono- and disaccharides</article-title><source>J Am Chem Soc</source><year>1979</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>1265</fpage><lpage>1274</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/ja00499a036</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Pfeffer PE, Valentine KM, Parrish FW (1979) Deuterium-induced differential isotope shift 13C NMR-resonance reassignments of mono- and disaccharides. J Am Chem Soc 101:1265&#x02013;1274 </citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prosen</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Radlein</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Piskorz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Microbial utilization of levoglucosan in wood pyrolysate as a carbon and energy source</article-title><source>Biotechnol Bioeng</source><year>1993</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>538</fpage><lpage>541</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/bit.260420419</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Prosen EM, Radlein D, Piskorz J, Scott DS (1993) Microbial utilization of levoglucosan in wood pyrolysate as a carbon and energy source. Biotechnol Bioeng 42:538&#x02013;541 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18613060</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pulz</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Photobioreactors: production systems for phototrophic microorganisms</article-title><source>Appl Microbiol Biotechnol</source><year>2001</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>287</fpage><lpage>293</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s002530100702</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Pulz O (2001) Photobioreactors: production systems for phototrophic microorganisms. Appl Microbiol Biotechnol 57:287&#x02013;293 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11759675</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pulz</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Gross</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Valuable products from biotechnology of microalgae</article-title><source>Appl Microbiol Biotechnol</source><year>2004</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>635</fpage><lpage>648</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00253-004-1647-x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Pulz O, Gross W (2004) Valuable products from biotechnology of microalgae. Appl Microbiol Biotechnol 65:635&#x02013;648 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15300417</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wikfors</surname><given-names>GH</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohno</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impact of algal research in aquaculture</article-title><source>J Phycol</source><year>2001</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>968</fpage><lpage>974</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1529-8817.2001.01136.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Wikfors GH, Ohno M (2001) Impact of algal research in aquaculture. J Phycol 37:968&#x02013;974 </citation></ref><ref id="CR21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>XQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Beardall</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallam</surname><given-names>ND</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modification of fatty acid composition in halophilic Antarctic microalgae</article-title><source>Phytochemistry</source><year>1998</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>1249</fpage><lpage>1252</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0031-9422(98)00117-4</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Xu XQ, Beardall J, Hallam ND (1998) Modification of fatty acid composition in halophilic Antarctic microalgae. Phytochemistry 49:1249&#x02013;1252 </citation></ref><ref id="CR22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhuang</surname><given-names>XL</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>HX</given-names></name><name><surname>Tang</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Levoglucosan kinase involved in citric acid fermentation by <italic>Aspergillus niger</italic> CBX-209 using levoglucosan as sole carbon and energy source</article-title><source>Biomass Bioenerg</source><year>2001</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0961-9534(01)00012-5</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Zhuang XL, Zhang HX, Tang JJ (2001) Levoglucosan kinase involved in citric acid fermentation by Aspergillus niger CBX-209 using levoglucosan as sole carbon and energy source. Biomass Bioenerg 21:53&#x02013;60 </citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>